      "title": "Center for Career & Professional Development",
      "description": "Center for Career & Professional Development | Centre College Skip to content Skip to AI Search Skip to main nav Search Keywords Log in Sign up Guests Access Handshake Make an appointment Who We Serve Alumni & Parents Employers Faculty & Staff Students Career Exploration Communities What is a CEC? Arts, Media & Entertainment Business & Finance Health & Medicine Law, Government & Policy Science, Engineering & Tech Social Impact Build Career Skills Apply to Grad School Create a Resume / Cover Letter Explore Your Interests Find an Internship Find a Job Interviewing Network with Centre Alumni Our Outcomes Meet the Team Meet the Staff Meet the Student Team Upcoming Events September Sep 04 Event: Register Here: 2026 SMBC Explore (for College Sophomores) Fri, Sep 4 from 10am - 4pm Friday, September 4th from 10am - 4pm Sep 08 Event: USPS - Automotive Technician Zoom Webinar - Memphis, TN Tue, Sep 8 from 10am - 11am Tuesday, September 8th from 10am - 11am Sep 08 Event: Lexington Police Cowan Table Tue, Sep 8 from 11:30am - 12:30pm Tuesday, September 8th from 11:30am - 12:30pm Sep 08 Event: GWI Ask Admissions: Open Q&A Session Tue, Sep 8 from 4pm - 4:45pm Tuesday, September 8th from 4pm - 4:45pm Sep 08 Event: Meet the Business - Wealth, U.S. Consumer Cards & Services (North America Session) Tue, Sep 8 from 5pm - 5:45pm Tuesday, September 8th from 5pm - 5:45pm Sep 08 Event: Kraft Heinz 101: Session 1 Tue, Sep 8 from 5pm - 6pm Tuesday, September 8th from 5pm - 6pm Sep 08 Event: Ankura Consulting - Ankura Office of the CFO® Virtual Information Session Tue, Sep 8 from 6pm - 7pm Tuesday, September 8th from 6pm - 7pm Sep 08 Event: Unlock Your Future: Banking Analyst Internships in Japan (North America) Tue, Sep 8 from 7pm - 8pm Tuesday, September 8th from 7pm - 8pm Sep 09 Event: Future in 15- Discover M&T Bank! Wed, Sep 9 from 10am - 10:15am Wednesday, September 9th from 10am - 10:15am Sep 09 Event: McKenney's Career Fair Prep Workshop! Wed, Sep 9 from 10am - 10:30am Wednesday, September 9th from 10am - 10:30am See more events News & Advice Career Resources Student Resources Jobs & Internships Career Videos Our Outcomes The Center for Career & Professional Development (CCPD) helps students and alumni plan, prepare, and promote their careers! Students Explore careers through personalized career coaching, experiential learning opportunities, and connecting with alumni and employers. Alumni Make a direct impact on students by helping them prepare for life after college. Career Exploration Communities (CECs) Join other Centre students with similar career interests to explore possible paths, participate in customized programming and events, network with industry insiders, and get the inside track on internships and jobs — all with the help of your own specialized career coach! THE STUDENT EXPERIENCE Jason Dias ’25 “Through their thought-provoking questions and expertise in prestigious graduate program admissions, the career coaches at Centre helped me leverage my story and career goals to earn admission into the Master of Accountancy at Vanderbilt with substantial financial aid.” Eleanor Grubbs ’24 “The CCPD and my career coach have helped me to refine my resume and prepare for job interviews countless times, as well as helped me to find 2 summer internships in my desired career field. In my opinion, it is one of the best resources to utilize on campus, a true hidden gem!” FOLLOW US ON SOCIAL MEDIA Instagram Facebook YouTube Sidebar Join or change your CEC LinkedIn Learning Job & Internship Opportunities Social Media Content Creator TOSOT Comfort Interior Design Intern DJ Designs, LLC Assistant Painting Supervisor AHRC NYC See All Jobs Career Resources Skip filter options to posts Filter Clear Filter: Filters See More Filters Filter Controls Resource Categories: Community Resources Cover Letter/Thank You Resources Employer Resources Faculty & Staff Resources Financial Aid How-tos & Support Guides Job Search Tools Networking Tools Online Tools Professional Associations Resume Resources Student Clubs & Organizations Student Highlighted Resources Close Clear Filters Academic Credit Internships Share This: Share Academic Credit Internships on Facebook Share Academic Credit Internships on LinkedIn Share Academic Credit Internships on X Copy Link Academic-credit internships require the supervision of a faculty member and an on-site supervisor, combining a substantive academic component with a … Read More Internship Learning Agreements Share This: Share Internship Learning Agreements on Facebook Share Internship Learning Agreements on LinkedIn Share Internship Learning Agreements on X Copy Link Centre College requires that students complete their internship learning agreements online through Docusign. This system allows students to complete contracts … Read More Non-Credit Internships Share This: Share Non-Credit Internships on Facebook Share Non-Credit Internships on LinkedIn Share Non-Credit Internships on X Copy Link Non-credit internships are those that do not receive academic credit and are often completed during the summer.  They do not … Read More Internship Funding Share This: Share Internship Funding on Facebook Share Internship Funding on LinkedIn Share Internship Funding on X Copy Link Centre College provides competitive financial support for students completing high-caliber unpaid or low-paid domestic or international internships during the CentreTerm … Read More Student Internship Guide Share This: Share Student Internship Guide on Facebook Share Student Internship Guide on LinkedIn Share Student Internship Guide on X Copy Link Centre College is proud to support internships during your time here. Internships are not only beneficial for future employment, but … Read More Writing Duties for an Internship vs. a Job Share This: Share Writing Duties for an Internship vs. a Job on Facebook Share Writing Duties for an Internship vs. a Job on LinkedIn Share Writing Duties for an Internship vs. a Job on X Copy Link Why the Difference Matters Job descriptions and internship descriptions should not sound identical. While both can involve meaningful work, internships … Read More View All Resources Career Videos How to ACTUALLY get an internship, as told by award winning interns Video post How to Land Internships and Entry Level Roles as an International Student Video post The Handshake Student Account Video post Prep Your Phone for Professional Life Video post Handshake 101 Video post Emerging Professionals: Skills for Surviving Corporate America Video post View All Videos Contact & Location Phone 859.238.5283 Email careers@centre.edu Address Old Carnegie, First floor 600 West Walnut Street Danville, KY 40422 CCPD Hours M Monday 8:30 am - 4:30 pm T Tuesday 8:30 am - 4:30 pm W Wednesday 8:30 am - 4:30 pm TH Thursday 8:30 am - 4:30 pm F Friday 8:30 am - 4:30 pm Meet the Team Jess Metzmeier Meet Jess Joy Asher Meet Joy Kirk Knott Meet Kirk Nate Meissner Meet Nate Lainy Castañeda Meet Lainy Kaitlyn Overstreet Meet Kaitlyn Michael Taylor Meet Michael Laura Hill Meet Laura Genny Ballard Meet Genny Bryana Miracle Meet Bryana Sherri Gowins Meet Sherri Phone 859.238.5283 Email careers@centre.edu Address Old Carnegie, First floor 600 West Walnut Street Danville, KY 40422 Facebook Instagram LinkedIn YouTube Footer Column 1 Blog Events Footer Column 2 Jobs & Internships Resources Meet the Team Privacy Policy | Terms of Service Copyright © 2026 Centre College"
