    "https://careers.centre.edu/resources/connect-with-us/": {
      "title": "Connect with Us",
      "description": "Connect with Us – Center for Career & Professional Development | Centre College Skip to content Skip to AI Search Skip to main nav Search Keywords Log in Sign up Guests Access Handshake Make an appointment Who We Serve Alumni & Parents Employers Faculty & Staff Students Career Exploration Communities What is a CEC? Arts, Media & Entertainment Business & Finance Health & Medicine Law, Government & Policy Science, Engineering & Tech Social Impact Build Career Skills Apply to Grad School Create a Resume / Cover Letter Explore Your Interests Find an Internship Find a Job Interviewing Network with Centre Alumni Our Outcomes Meet the Team Meet the Staff Meet the Student Team Connect with Us Share This: Share Connect with Us on Facebook Share Connect with Us on LinkedIn Share Connect with Us on X Copy Link We’re here to help students and alumni apply for internships, jobs and graduate school, as well as explore your career options and interests. We want to help you succeed in whatever endeavors you choose to pursue! How to Make an Appointment with Us The CCPD offers both in-person and virtual appointments. Students may make an appointment with a Career Coach online using the links below or drop by to see a Career Peer Mentor. If you have general questions or aren’t sure who your career coach is, call 859-238-5283 or email careers@centre.edu . Career Peer Mentors Career Peer Mentors are also here to help! They can get you started on a resume, help find resources for your internship/job/grad school search, help you apply for internship funding, and answer quick questions you might have. Drop by during office hours for assistance—no appointment necessary! Career Peer Mentor Drop-in Hours Monday: 9:30 – 11:30 a.m., 12:30 – 1:30 p.m., and 3:00 – 4:00 p.m. Tuesday: 11:30 – 1:30 p.m. Wednesday: 10:00 – 12:00 p.m., and 3:00 – 4:00 p.m. Thursday: 9:30 – 1:30 p.m. Friday: 10:00 – 12:00 p.m., and 3:00 – 4:00 p.m. Schedule with a Career Peer Mentor Career Coaches Below are our career coaches and the Career Exploration Communities (CECs) they serve. You can make an appointment with either coach based on the CECs you’re a member of. Kirk Knott Science, Engineering & Tech CEC Social Impact CEC Schedule an Appointment with Kirk Nate Meissner Arts, Media & Entertainment CEC Law, Government & Policy CEC Schedule an Appointment with Nate Lainy Castañeda Health & Medicine CEC Schedule an Appointment with Lainy Kaitlyn Overstreet Business & Finance CEC Schedule an Appointment with Kaitlyn Contact & Location Phone 859.238.5283 Email careers@centre.edu Address Old Carnegie, First floor 600 West Walnut Street Danville, KY 40422 CCPD Hours M Monday 8:30 am - 4:30 pm T Tuesday 8:30 am - 4:30 pm W Wednesday 8:30 am - 4:30 pm TH Thursday 8:30 am - 4:30 pm F Friday 8:30 am - 4:30 pm Meet the Team Jess Metzmeier Meet Jess Joy Asher Meet Joy Kirk Knott Meet Kirk Nate Meissner Meet Nate Lainy Castañeda Meet Lainy Kaitlyn Overstreet Meet Kaitlyn Michael Taylor Meet Michael Laura Hill Meet Laura Genny Ballard Meet Genny Bryana Miracle Meet Bryana Sherri Gowins Meet Sherri Phone 859.238.5283 Email careers@centre.edu Address Old Carnegie, First floor 600 West Walnut Street Danville, KY 40422 Facebook Instagram LinkedIn YouTube Footer Column 1 Blog Events Footer Column 2 Jobs & Internships Resources Meet the Team Privacy Policy | Terms of Service Copyright © 2026 Centre College"
    },
    "https://careers.centre.edu/channels/alumni/": {
      "title": "Alumni & Parents",
      "description": "Alumni & Parents – Center for Career & Professional Development | Centre College Skip to content Skip to AI Search Skip to main nav Search Keywords Log in Sign up Guests Access Handshake Make an appointment Who We Serve Alumni & Parents Employers Faculty & Staff Students Career Exploration Communities What is a CEC? Arts, Media & Entertainment Business & Finance Health & Medicine Law, Government & Policy Science, Engineering & Tech Social Impact Build Career Skills Apply to Grad School Create a Resume / Cover Letter Explore Your Interests Find an Internship Find a Job Interviewing Network with Centre Alumni Our Outcomes Meet the Team Meet the Staff Meet the Student Team News & Advice Career Resources Student Resources Jobs & Internships Career Videos Our Outcomes Alumni & Parents Centre alumni and parents can make a direct and lasting impact on students by helping them prepare for life after college. Whether mentoring students through our Career Advocates program, sponsoring an internship, or connecting students with job opportunities, you can give back to Centre students in a way that will positively impact them for the rest of their lives! Become a Career Advocate Helping current students succeed is the heart of the Centre experience. Career Advocates are alumni  and parents actively committed to helping students explore and launch careers. Centre Career Advocates: Give information and advice on how to prepare and succeed in their career field Share first-hand tips on interviewing or preparing grad-school applications Provide shadowing opportunities Serve as speakers for on-campus or virtual panels and presentation And more! WHAT STUDENTS ARE SAYING Caroline Schoenig ’24 “My Career Advocate provided in-depth knowledge about her job and company. So much so that I now work at her company as a consultant.” Suzanne Bicksler ’25 “My Career Advocate helped me prepare for an interview and gave me inside knowledge about the company’s needs which made the process simpler.” WHAT CAREER ADVOCATES ARE SAYING Robertson Nash ’83 Director, HIV Program, Tennessee Department of Health “I always enjoy the opportunity to lend a hand to a fellow Centre Colonel. I know that I’m going to be connecting someone from my network with a bright, articulate, and thoughtful person. Centre continues to equip students with the same gifts that have stood me in good stead throughout my career. There’s just no substitute for strong critical thinking skills grounded in a world view that encourages optimism and service to others.” Dr. Abby Winterberg-Hess ’05 Nurse Practitioner and Clinical Researcher, Cincinnati Children’s Hospital Medical Center “Making connections through the career advocate program can help open doors to opportunities that you may not have known existed. These type of connections have made a huge impact for me personally throughout my career. As a career advocate for Centre, I really enjoy helping students as they begin the journey to finding a career pathway that aligns with their interests, talents and passion.” Sign up to be a Career Advocate Provide Career Opportunities Centre alumni and parents are uniquely positioned to provide internship and job opportunities for our students!  If you’d like to hire a Centre student for an internship or job, click the Sponsor a Job or Internship button to connect with Joy Asher, or email her directly .  She can post your opportunity and create a customized plan for connecting you with the best-fit students.  If you would like to post directly through Handshake or you’d like to come to campus to engage with our students, visit our Employer page for more information. Sponsor a Job or Internship Are You an Alumnus Searching for a Job or Applying to Grad School? We are here for you! Connect with us to get help on the next steps of your career journey. Sidebar Sponsor a Job or Internship Sign up to be a Career Advocate Connect with Us Jess Metzmeier Meet Jess Career Resources Skip filter options to posts Filter Clear Filter: Filters See More Filters Filter Controls Resource Categories: Community Resources Cover Letter/Thank You Resources Employer Resources Faculty & Staff Resources Financial Aid How-tos & Support Guides Job Search Tools Networking Tools Online Tools Professional Associations Resume Resources Student Clubs & Organizations Student Highlighted Resources Close Clear Filters Handshake Share This: Share Handshake on Facebook Share Handshake on LinkedIn Share Handshake on X Copy Link Handshake is Centre College’s online job and internship posting system, which allows jobs to be filtered towards your major, minor … Read More Salary Expert: Cost of Living Calculator Share This: Share Salary Expert: Cost of Living Calculator on Facebook Share Salary Expert: Cost of Living Calculator on LinkedIn Share Salary Expert: Cost of Living Calculator on X Copy Link Compare salaries from one location to the next (tip: enter 0 when asked for observation of costs). View Resource Career InfoNet Share This: Share Career InfoNet on Facebook Share Career InfoNet on LinkedIn Share Career InfoNet on X Copy Link Comprehensive information on states, wages, and salary and job trends. View Resource GlassDoor Share This: Share GlassDoor on Facebook Share GlassDoor on LinkedIn Share GlassDoor on X Copy Link Get inside information on companies including salaries, reviews, and interviews; all posted by employees. View Resource View All Resources Career Videos Networking & Professionalism Video post Does Your Major Determine Your Career Path? Video post View All Videos Contact & Location Phone 859.238.5283 Email careers@centre.edu Address Old Carnegie, First floor 600 West Walnut Street Danville, KY 40422 CCPD Hours M Monday 8:30 am - 4:30 pm T Tuesday 8:30 am - 4:30 pm W Wednesday 8:30 am - 4:30 pm TH Thursday 8:30 am - 4:30 pm F Friday 8:30 am - 4:30 pm Meet the Team Jess Metzmeier Meet Jess Joy Asher Meet Joy Kirk Knott Meet Kirk Nate Meissner Meet Nate Lainy Castañeda Meet Lainy Kaitlyn Overstreet Meet Kaitlyn Michael Taylor Meet Michael Laura Hill Meet Laura Genny Ballard Meet Genny Bryana Miracle Meet Bryana Sherri Gowins Meet Sherri Phone 859.238.5283 Email careers@centre.edu Address Old Carnegie, First floor 600 West Walnut Street Danville, KY 40422 Facebook Instagram LinkedIn YouTube Footer Column 1 Blog Events Footer Column 2 Jobs & Internships Resources Meet the Team Privacy Policy | Terms of Service Copyright © 2026 Centre College"
