    "https://careers.centre.edu/channels/student/": {
      "title": "Students",
      "description": "Students – Center for Career & Professional Development | Centre College Skip to content Skip to AI Search Skip to main nav Search Keywords Log in Sign up Guests Access Handshake Make an appointment Who We Serve Alumni & Parents Employers Faculty & Staff Students Career Exploration Communities What is a CEC? Arts, Media & Entertainment Business & Finance Health & Medicine Law, Government & Policy Science, Engineering & Tech Social Impact Build Career Skills Apply to Grad School Create a Resume / Cover Letter Explore Your Interests Find an Internship Find a Job Interviewing Network with Centre Alumni Our Outcomes Meet the Team Meet the Staff Meet the Student Team News & Advice Career Resources Student Resources Jobs & Internships Career Videos Our Outcomes Students Let’s Get Started Starting your career exploration can be overwhelming, but that’s where we come in! Take a look at our services below that are meant to guide you through exploring and choosing careers, connect you with alumni, provide you with skills needed to achieve success, and help with experiential learning through internships and research. Instagram Facebook YouTube Twitter Career Peer Mentors Students can start here by meeting with a Career Peer Mentor. CPMs meet with students individually and in groups, providing services including resume reviews, internship search assistance, and graduate school information for each of the Career Exploration Communities (CECs). View Career Peer Mentor Drop-in Hours Career Coaching Career Coaches provide a deeper dive into your career exploration by helping students decide on a major; take self-assessments; write resumes and personal statements; locate and apply to internships, research opportunities, post-grad jobs, and graduate school; and much more. Make an appointment with a Career Coach Career Exploration Communities Student are encouraged join the Career Exploration Communities (CECs) to help provide substantial career support and success. You can join one or more communities to explore an array of careers through customized programs and events, networking, and specialized internships.  Faculty, staff, Career Advocates, and industry experts provide advice and mentorship. Learn more about CECs Find an Internship Khatibah Adesanya ’26 managed the production of microalgae and brine shrimp at the NovAquatik as an Aquarium Assistant in Mérida, Yucatán, México. Joao Azevedo ’24 conducted research for temporary exhibitions at The American Family Immigration History Center (AFIHC) as a Research Assistant in New York, NY. Elizabeth Fortress ’25 solidified her decision of being a family physician after a “life changing experience” at Ephraim McDowell as a Medical Office Intern.⁠ Learn more about internships Sidebar Upcoming Events September Sep 04 Event: Register Here: 2026 SMBC Explore (for College Sophomores) Fri, Sep 4 from 10am - 4pm Friday, September 4th from 10am - 4pm Sep 08 Event: USPS - Automotive Technician Zoom Webinar - Memphis, TN Tue, Sep 8 from 10am - 11am Tuesday, September 8th from 10am - 11am Sep 08 Event: Lexington Police Cowan Table Tue, Sep 8 from 11:30am - 12:30pm Tuesday, September 8th from 11:30am - 12:30pm Sep 08 Event: GWI Ask Admissions: Open Q&A Session Tue, Sep 8 from 4pm - 4:45pm Tuesday, September 8th from 4pm - 4:45pm Sep 08 Event: Meet the Business - Wealth, U.S. Consumer Cards & Services (North America Session) Tue, Sep 8 from 5pm - 5:45pm Tuesday, September 8th from 5pm - 5:45pm View More Connect with Us Kaitlyn Overstreet Meet Kaitlyn Kirk Knott Meet Kirk Lainy Castañeda Meet Lainy Nate Meissner Meet Nate Network with Centre Alumni Student Resources Skip filter options to posts Filter Clear Filter: Filters See More Filters Filter Controls Resource Categories: Community Resources Cover Letter/Thank You Resources Employer Resources Faculty & Staff Resources Financial Aid How-tos & Support Guides Job Search Tools Networking Tools Online Tools Professional Associations Resume