    "https://careers.centre.edu/what-is-a-cec/": {
      "title": "What is a CEC?",
      "description": "What is a CEC? – Center for Career & Professional Development | Centre College Skip to content Skip to AI Search Skip to main nav Search Keywords Log in Sign up Guests Access Handshake Make an appointment Who We Serve Alumni & Parents Employers Faculty & Staff Students Career Exploration Communities What is a CEC? Arts, Media & Entertainment Business & Finance Health & Medicine Law, Government & Policy Science, Engineering & Tech Social Impact Build Career Skills Apply to Grad School Create a Resume / Cover Letter Explore Your Interests Find an Internship Find a Job Interviewing Network with Centre Alumni Our Outcomes Meet the Team Meet the Staff Meet the Student Team News & Advice Career Resources Student Resources Jobs & Internships Career Videos Our Outcomes What is a CEC? Helping Centre students discover what’s next Join other Centre students with similar career interests to explore possible paths, participate in customized programming and events, network with industry insiders, and get the inside track on internships and jobs — all with the help of your own specialized career coach! You will learn how to create a personalized plan for exploring careers, gaining experience, and applying to jobs as well as graduate schools. Career Exploration Communities (CEC) will lay the foundation for your career readiness and success after Centre. Students can join as many of the six CECs as they’d like, and can switch when needed as they move throughout their career journey. We encourage you to pick a primary CEC, though, as that will help specify your career coach and exploration. CECs and their careers Arts, Media & Entertainment – Performing arts including fine arts; music; dance and drama; arts administration and production; art and history museums; humanities; writing, editing, and journalism; advertising; communication; public relations; architecture; television, radio and film media including on-air and production; sports; distilleries; and entertainment venues. Business & Finance – All business fields including marketing, sales, consulting, real estate, finance and banking, investing and wealth management, accounting, manufacturing, logistics and commerce, and entrepreneurship. Health & Medicine – All medical fields including MD and DO; physician assistant; nurse and nurse practitioner; EMT/paramedic; medical research; physical, occupational and speech-language therapy; chiropractic; public health; and veterinary. Law, Government & Policy – Law and law enforcement, politics, lobbying, government and international relations, public affairs and public policy. Science, Engineering & Tech – Life, physical and environmental science; research; engineering (all fields); mathematics; data science and data analytics; computer programming; technology and AI; and software engineering and development. Social Impact – Education (preschool, k-12, and higher ed), community service and engagement, religion/ministry, non-profit, sustainability, psychology and mental health counseling, social work, and social justice. Personalized Career Coaching A career coach can help you in your search for internships, jobs, and graduate schools. They offer mock interviews, assistance with resume and cover letter writing, as well as connections to alumni who are ready and willing to help you in your career exploration. Join a CEC LinkedIn Group For every CEC there is a LinkedIn group that students can join where they’ll be notified of job and internship opportunities, events, and be able to network with alumni. Sign up for or change CEC Find the Right Fit Having trouble deciding which community is right for you? Take our CEC Quiz. Take the CEC quiz Meet the Career Coaches Kirk Knott Associate Director, Lead Career Coach Kirk provides career coaching to students in the Science, Engineering & Tech and Social Impact CECs, as well as alumni and all undecided students. Schedule an Appointment via Calendly Schedule an Appointment via Navigate Nate Meissner Senior Assistant Director, Career Coach Nate provides career coaching to students in the Arts, Media & Entertainment, and Law, Government & Policy CECs. Schedule an Appointment via Calendly Schedule an Appointment via Navigate Lainy Castañeda Assistant Director, Career Coach Lainy provides career coaching to students in the Health & Medicine CEC. Schedule an Appointment via Calendly Schedule an Appointment via Navigate Kaitlyn Overstreet Assistant Director, Career Coach Kaitlyn provides career coaching to students in the Business & Finance CEC. Schedule an Appointment via Calendly Schedule an Appointment via Navigate Internship Opportunities Social Media Content Creator TOSOT Comfort Interior Design Intern DJ Designs, LLC Talent Acquisition Intern (TikTok Shop) - 2027 Summer TikTok Inc. Data Analyst Intern - Summer 2027 McKesson McKesson Health Systems (MHS) Marketing Intern - Summer 2027 McKesson Operations Graduate Program Amgen See All Internships Job Opportunities Assistant Painting Supervisor AHRC NYC Remote Personal Assistant Thomsen Holman Wheiler, PLLC Behavioral Specialist -- Be the Difference in Someone's Journey (Part Time) Monarch Controller NEW Health Programs Association Interventional Radiology Technologist – Acute Care – Full time MU Health Care See All Jobs Career Videos Mini Career Chat: Environmental and Sustainability Video post Mini Career Chat: Education Video post Genetics Career Chat Video post UX Design Career Chat Video post Software Engineering Employer Panel Video post Mini Career Chat: Lobbyist Video post View All Videos Contact & Location Phone 859.238.5283 Email careers@centre.edu Address Old Carnegie, First floor 600 West Walnut Street Danville, KY 40422 CCPD Hours M Monday 8:30 am - 4:30 pm T Tuesday 8:30 am - 4:30 pm W Wednesday 8:30 am - 4:30 pm TH Thursday 8:30 am - 4:30 pm F Friday 8:30 am - 4:30 pm Meet the Team Jess Metzmeier Meet Jess Joy Asher Meet Joy Kirk Knott Meet Kirk Nate Meissner Meet Nate Lainy Castañeda