    "https://careers.centre.edu/channels/search-for-an-internship/": {
      "title": "Find an Internship",
      "description": "Find an Internship – Center for Career & Professional Development | Centre College Skip to content Skip to AI Search Skip to main nav Search Keywords Log in Sign up Guests Access Handshake Make an appointment Who We Serve Alumni & Parents Employers Faculty & Staff Students Career Exploration Communities What is a CEC? Arts, Media & Entertainment Business & Finance Health & Medicine Law, Government & Policy Science, Engineering & Tech Social Impact Build Career Skills Apply to Grad School Create a Resume / Cover Letter Explore Your Interests Find an Internship Find a Job Interviewing Network with Centre Alumni Our Outcomes Meet the Team Meet the Staff Meet the Student Team News & Advice Career Resources Student Resources Jobs & Internships Career Videos Our Outcomes Find an Internship Internships give students clarity and confidence in their career choice and provide invaluable, necessary experience for post-graduate success. Internships provide hands-on experiential learning opportunities where students apply classroom knowledge to real-life situations, developing skills in a professional setting. Students can participate in academic credit internships during the fall, CentreTerm, spring, or summer, and in non-credit internships during the summer. The CCPD can connect students with an array of internship opportunities. Click this button for a full list of internships for Centre students on Handshake. View All Internships In addition to these opportunities, our career coaches can connect students directly with Centre alumni offering internships just for Centre students! Search by Area of Study or Interest If you’d like to focus your internship search by career field, there are a variety of internship resources for each Career Exploration Community (CEC) below. Simply click on your CEC, then scroll down that page to the Internship Resources section under Career Resources. Arts, Media & Entertainment Business & Finance Health & Medicine Law, Government & Policy Science, Engineering & Tech Social Impact Search by Location Click below to search for internships in some of our most popular locations. This is not an all-inclusive list, and you can filter your search for other locations on Handshake . Atlanta Cincinnati Lexington Louisville Nashville New York City Washington D.C. Follow Interns on Instagram Kaylen Storms ’24 learned the operations of how a non-profit organization runs, indulged in community coordination and communication as an Outreach Intern with Bluegrass Greensource in Lexington, KY. Cindy Zamarripa ’24 gained insight working in academia using two languages as an Editorial Assistant with Ñawpa Pacha: Journal of the Institute of Andean Studies. What Is an Internship? NACE (the National Association of Colleges and Employers) defines an internship as a form of experiential learning that integrates knowledge and theory learned in the classroom with practical application and skills development in a professional workplace setting. Internships provide students the opportunity to gain valuable applied experience, develop social capital, explore career fields, and make connections in professional fields. A learning experience with a real-world opportunity to apply the knowledge gained in the classroom. It must not be simply to advance the operations of the employer or replace the work that a regular employee would routinely perform. Learned skills and knowledge that are transferable to other employment settings. A defined beginning and end that is mutually agreed upon and consistent with institutional sponsor guidelines and schedules. A position description with clear responsibilities and required/desired qualifications. Clearly defined learning objectives/goals supportive of the student’s academic program goals and institutional requirements. Direct supervision by a professional(s) with relevant expertise and educational and/or professional experience who provides productive feedback, guidance, and the resources and equipment necessary to successfully complete the assignment. Why Do an Internship? The chance to apply knowledge from class in real-life situations The opportunity to “test drive” a possible career and find out if it suits you Professional contacts who often prove helpful when you’re searching for a job after graduation Relevant job experience and an enhanced resume, making you more marketable to employers Possible academic credit on your transcript How Do I Get an Internship? Setting up an internship at Centre is simple. Students pursue academic internships during their sophomore, junior, or senior year and may participate in non-credit internships at any point in their time at Centre. If participating in a credit internship, they choose a faculty advisor and, with the help of the Center for Career & Professional Development (CCPD), find and apply to an internship site. Together, the student, the faculty advisor, and the intern sponsor set expectations for the internship. Where Will I Intern? Here’s a sampling of organizations where Centre students have recently completed internships: Amazon Art Academy London Bank of America Baptist Health Brown-Forman CASA (Court Appointed Special Advocates) Catholic Charities, Diocese of Nashville Cincinnati Children’s Hospital Cleveland Browns Clinica de Merida (Mexico) Ernst & Young Field Museum First Southern National Bank Florida State Attorney’s Office Foundation for International Medical Relief of Children Humana International Rescue Committee Japan America Society of Kentucky KMS Technology Lockheed Martin Louisville Zoo Massachusetts General Hospital McCarthy Strategic Solutions Mercer Microsoft National Football League National Museum of Ghana Norton Healthcare Ohio First District Court of Appeals PT Pros RJ Corman The Statue of Liberty – Ellis Island Foundation United States Department of Veterans Affairs United States Golf Association United States House of Representatives United States Trade and Development Agency Vanderbilt University Medical Center Sidebar Connect with Us Kaitlyn Overstreet Meet Kaitlyn Kirk Knott Meet Kirk Lainy Castañeda Meet Lainy Nate Meissner Meet Nate Career Resources Skip filter options to posts Filter Clear Filter: Filters See More Filters Filter Controls Resource Categories: Community Resources Cover Letter/Thank You Resources Employer Resources Faculty & Staff Resources Financial Aid How-tos & Support Guides Job Search Tools Networking Tools Online Tools Professional Associations Resume Resources Student Clubs & Organizations Student Highlighted Resources Close Clear Filters Academic Credit Internships Share This: Share Academic Credit Internships on Facebook Share Academic Credit Internships on LinkedIn Share Academic Credit Internships on X Copy Link Academic-credit internships require the supervision of a faculty member and an on-site supervisor, combining a substantive academic component with a … Read More Internship Learning Agreements Share This: Share Internship Learning Agreements on Facebook Share Internship Learning Agreements on LinkedIn Share Internship Learning Agreements on X Copy Link Centre College requires that students complete their internship learning agreements online through Docusign. This system allows students to complete contracts … Read More Non-Credit Internships Share This: Share Non-Credit Internships on Facebook Share Non-Credit Internships on LinkedIn Share Non-Credit Internships on X Copy Link Non-credit internships are those that do not receive academic credit and are often completed during the summer.  They do not … Read More Internship Funding Share This: Share Internship Funding on Facebook Share Internship Funding on LinkedIn Share Internship Funding on X Copy Link Centre College provides competitive financial support for students completing high-caliber unpaid or low-paid domestic or international internships during the CentreTerm … Read More Student Internship Guide Share This: Share Student Internship Guide on Facebook Share Student Internship Guide on LinkedIn Share Student Internship Guide on X Copy Link Centre College is proud to support internships during your time here. Internships are not only beneficial for future employment, but … Read More Writing Duties for an Internship vs. a Job Share This: Share Writing Duties for an Internship vs. a Job on Facebook Share Writing Duties for an Internship vs. a Job on LinkedIn Share Writing Duties for an Internship vs. a Job on X Copy Link Why the Difference Matters Job descriptions and internship descriptions should not sound identical. While both can involve meaningful work, internships … Read More View All Resources Career Videos How to ACTUALLY get an internship, as told by award winning interns Video post How to Land Internships and Entry Level Roles as an International Student Video post Prep Your Phone for Professional Life Video post Handshake 101 Video post View All Videos Contact & Location Phone 859.238.5283 Email careers@centre.edu Address Old Carnegie, First floor 600 West Walnut Street Danville, KY 40422 CCPD Hours M Monday 8:30 am - 4:30 pm T Tuesday 8:30 am - 4:30 pm W Wednesday 8:30 am - 4:30 pm TH Thursday 8:30 am - 4:30 pm F Friday 8:30 am - 4:30 pm Meet the Team Jess Metzmeier Meet Jess Joy Asher Meet Joy Kirk Knott Meet Kirk Nate Meissner Meet Nate Lainy Castañeda Meet Lainy Kaitlyn Overstreet Meet Kaitlyn Michael Taylor Meet Michael Laura Hill Meet Laura Genny Ballard Meet Genny Bryana Miracle Meet Bryana Sherri Gowins Meet Sherri Phone 859.238.5283 Email careers@centre.edu Address Old Carnegie, First floor 600 West Walnut Street Danville, KY 40422 Facebook Instagram LinkedIn YouTube Footer Column 1 Blog Events Footer Column 2 Jobs & Internships Resources Meet the Team Privacy Policy | Terms of Service Copyright © 2026 Centre College"
