    "https://careers.centre.edu/channels/search-for-a-job/": {
      "title": "Find a Job",
      "description": "Find a Job – Center for Career & Professional Development | Centre College Skip to content Skip to AI Search Skip to main nav Search Keywords Log in Sign up Guests Access Handshake Make an appointment Who We Serve Alumni & Parents Employers Faculty & Staff Students Career Exploration Communities What is a CEC? Arts, Media & Entertainment Business & Finance Health & Medicine Law, Government & Policy Science, Engineering & Tech Social Impact Build Career Skills Apply to Grad School Create a Resume / Cover Letter Explore Your Interests Find an Internship Find a Job Interviewing Network with Centre Alumni Our Outcomes Meet the Team Meet the Staff Meet the Student Team News & Advice Career Resources Student Resources Jobs & Internships Career Videos Our Outcomes Find a Job The Center for Career & Professional Development is here to help you in your job search!  See below for job search resources or make an appointment with a Career Peer Mentor to get started. View All Jobs Search by Area of Study or Interest If you’d like to focus your job search by career field, there are a variety of job search resources for each Career Exploration Community (CEC) below. Simply click on your CEC, then scroll down that page to the Employment Resources section under Career Resources. Arts, Media & Entertainment Business & Finance Health & Medicine Law, Government & Policy Science, Engineering & Tech Social Impact Handshake is Centre College’s online job and internship posting system, which allows jobs to be filtered towards your major, minor and coursework and allows for you to view and sign-up for on-campus events in a more convenient way. All current students have access to their Handshake accounts. Join Handshake Tailor Jobs and Internships on Handshake Search LinkedIn You can use LinkedIn to find the right job or internship, connect and strengthen professional relationships, and learn the skills you need to succeed in your career. Sidebar Connect with Us Awa Nialing Drame Meet Awa Nialing Abhishek Basnet Meet Abhishek Karla Carrillo Meet Karla Kennedy Ushiroda Send an Email Career Resources Skip filter options to posts Filter Clear Filter: Filters See More Filters Filter Controls Resource Categories: Community Resources Cover Letter/Thank You Resources Employer Resources Faculty & Staff Resources Financial Aid How-tos & Support Guides Job Search Tools Networking Tools Online Tools Professional Associations Resume Resources Student Clubs & Organizations Student Highlighted Resources Close Clear Filters NUMBEO (Cost of Living) Share This: Share NUMBEO (Cost of Living) on Facebook Share NUMBEO (Cost of Living) on LinkedIn Share NUMBEO (Cost of Living) on X Copy Link Numbeo is the world’s largest cost-of-living and quality-of-life database. It covers housing, healthcare, transport, and other key indicators used by … Read More LinkedIn Learning Share This: Share LinkedIn Learning on Facebook Share LinkedIn Learning on LinkedIn Share LinkedIn Learning on X Copy Link If you’d like to work on building your skills on your own time in the trusted hands of industry experts … Read More Futuriti Share This: Share Futuriti on Facebook Share Futuriti on LinkedIn Share Futuriti on X Copy Link Are you exploring career opportunities in Kentucky? Find careers that match your skills and interests, and learn what you need … Read More Identify Fraudulent Jobs Opportunities Share This: Share Identify Fraudulent Jobs Opportunities on Facebook Share Identify Fraudulent Jobs Opportunities on LinkedIn Share Identify Fraudulent Jobs Opportunities on X Copy Link Scammers often use job opportunities to collect personal information, so it’s important to learn how to differentiate legitimate job listings … Read More Social Media Tips for Job Seeking College Students Share This: Share Social Media Tips for Job Seeking College Students on Facebook Share Social Media Tips for Job Seeking College Students on LinkedIn Share Social Media Tips for Job Seeking College Students on X Copy Link According to a CareerBuilder survey, 70% of employers use social media to screen candidates. Below are some social media tips … Read More Forage Share This: Share Forage on Facebook Share Forage on LinkedIn Share Forage on X Copy Link Explore careers and prepare for the job with hundreds of free job simulations designed by the world’s top employers. View Resource View All Resources Career Videos The Handshake Student Account Video post Prep Your Phone for Professional Life Video post Handshake 101 Video post Emerging Professionals: Skills for Surviving Corporate America Video post Elevate Your Career with P.I.E Video post View All Videos Contact & Location Phone 859.238.5283 Email careers@centre.edu Address Old Carnegie, First floor 600 West Walnut Street Danville, KY 40422 CCPD Hours M Monday 8:30 am - 4:30 pm T Tuesday 8:30 am - 4:30 pm W Wednesday 8:30 am - 4:30 pm TH Thursday 8:30 am - 4:30 pm F Friday 8:30 am - 4:30 pm Meet the Team Jess Metzmeier Meet Jess Joy Asher Meet Joy Kirk Knott Meet Kirk Nate Meissner Meet Nate Lainy Castañeda Meet Lainy Kaitlyn Overstreet Meet Kaitlyn Michael Taylor Meet Michael Laura Hill Meet Laura Genny Ballard Meet Genny Bryana Miracle Meet Bryana Sherri Gowins Meet Sherri Phone 859.238.5283 Email careers@centre.edu Address Old Carnegie, First floor 600 West Walnut Street Danville, KY 40422 Facebook Instagram LinkedIn YouTube Footer Column 1 Blog Events Footer Column 2 Jobs & Internships Resources Meet the Team Privacy Policy | Terms of Service Copyright © 2026 Centre College"
    },
    "https://careers.centre.edu/channels/interviewing/": {
      "title": "Interviewing",
      "description": "Interviewing – Center for Career & Professional Development | Centre College Skip to content Skip to AI Search Skip to main nav Search Keywords Log in Sign up Guests Access Handshake Make an appointment Who We Serve Alumni & Parents Employers Faculty & Staff Students Career Exploration Communities What is a CEC? Arts, Media & Entertainment Business & Finance Health & Medicine Law, Government & Policy Science, Engineering & Tech Social Impact Build Career Skills Apply to Grad School Create a Resume / Cover Letter Explore Your Interests Find an Internship Find a Job Interviewing Network with Centre Alumni Our Outcomes Meet the Team Meet the Staff Meet the Student Team News & Advice Career Resources Student Resources Jobs & Internships Career Videos Our Outcomes Interviewing Proper preparation will help alleviate some of the stress involved in interviewing for jobs. The more you prepare, the more comfortable and successful you will be interviewing. So, what can you do to ensure that you are ready for your interview? Schedule a Mock Interview Practice Practice answering interview questions and practice your responses to typical job interview questions (both general and industry-specific). Providing evidence of your successes is a great way to promote your candidacy, so think of concrete examples you can use to highlight your skills. Prepare a list of your own questions to ask the employer. Once you have practiced answering interview questions on your own, schedule a mock interview with the Center for Career & Professional Development so that we can help you hone your interviewing skills. Research Prior to the interview, find out who you will be meeting with so that you can research them beforehand. Do your homework about the employer and the industry so you are ready for the question “What do you know about this company?” Try to relate what you have learned about the company when answering questions. Also be sure that you thoroughly understand the job description and what skills the employer is seeking, so that you can relate your experience to their needs. Research with Forage Explore careers and prepare for the job with hundreds of free job simulations designed by the world’s top employers. You can also access Forage through your Navigate homepage! Get started Present a Professional Image Make sure your interview attire is neat and appropriate to the position. Bring a nice portfolio with copies of your resume. Include a pen and paper for taking notes (if you choose to do so). When greeting the employer, have a firm, confident handshake. Don’t Be Late Be on time for the interview, meaning five to ten minutes early. If needed, drive to the interview location ahead of time so you know where you are going and how long it will take to get there. Relax During the job interview try to relax and stay as calm possible. Remember that your body language says as much about you as your answers to the questions. Proper preparation will allow you to exude confidence. Maintain eye contact with the interviewer. Listen to the entire question before you answer and be sure to answer each question fully yet succinctly. Apply Your Skills and Knowledge Try to relate what you know about the company when answering questions. When discussing your career accomplishments match them to what the company is looking for. Use examples from your research when answering questions, such as “I noticed that when you implemented a new software system last year, your customer satisfaction ratings improved dramatically. I am well versed in the latest technologies from my experience with developing software at ABC, and appreciate a company who strives to be a leader in its industry.” Follow Up Always follow-up with a thank you note reiterating your interest in the position. You can also include any details you may have forgotten to mention during your interview. If you interview with multiple people, send each one a personal thank you note. Send your thank you note/email within 24 hours of your interview. Sidebar Career Resources Skip filter options to posts Filter Clear Filter: Filters See More Filters Filter Controls Resource Categories: Community Resources Cover Letter/Thank You Resources Employer Resources Faculty & Staff Resources Financial Aid How-tos & Support Guides Job Search Tools Networking Tools Online Tools Professional Associations Resume Resources Student Clubs & Organizations Student Highlighted Resources Close Clear Filters Discussing Salary & Benefits Share This: Share Discussing Salary & Benefits on Facebook Share Discussing Salary & Benefits on LinkedIn Share Discussing Salary & Benefits on X Copy Link Avoid discussing the salary or benefits offered for a position until given this information by the employer. Asking how much … Read More Sample Interview Questions Share This: Share Sample Interview Questions on Facebook Share Sample Interview Questions on LinkedIn Share Sample Interview Questions on X Copy Link View Resource Types of Interviews and How to Prepare Share This: Share Types of Interviews and How to Prepare on Facebook Share Types of Interviews and How to Prepare on LinkedIn Share Types of Interviews and How to Prepare on X Copy Link There are a few different types of interviews and interview questions. Understanding the structure and purpose of each can help … Read More View All Resources Career Videos Technical Interview Video post How to follow up after a job interview and say thank you Video post In-Person Interviewing Video post View All Videos Contact & Location Phone 859.238.5283 Email careers@centre.edu Address Old Carnegie, First floor 600 West Walnut Street Danville, KY 40422 CCPD Hours M Monday 8:30 am - 4:30 pm T Tuesday 8:30 am - 4:30 pm W Wednesday 8:30 am - 4:30 pm TH Thursday 8:30 am - 4:30 pm F Friday 8:30 am - 4:30 pm Meet the Team Jess Metzmeier Meet Jess Joy Asher Meet Joy Kirk Knott Meet Kirk Nate Meissner Meet Nate Lainy Castañeda Meet Lainy Kaitlyn Overstreet Meet Kaitlyn Michael Taylor Meet Michael Laura Hill Meet Laura Genny Ballard Meet Genny Bryana Miracle Meet Bryana Sherri Gowins Meet Sherri Phone 859.238.5283 Email careers@centre.edu Address Old Carnegie, First floor 600 West Walnut Street Danville, KY 40422 Facebook Instagram LinkedIn YouTube Footer Column 1 Blog Events Footer Column 2 Jobs & Internships Resources Meet the Team Privacy Policy | Terms of Service Copyright © 2026 Centre College"
    },
    "https://careers.centre.edu/channels/expand-your-network-mentor/": {
      "title": "Network with Centre Alumni",
      "description": "Network with Centre Alumni – Center for Career & Professional Development | Centre College Skip to content Skip to AI Search Skip to main nav Search Keywords Log in Sign up Guests Access Handshake Make an appointment Who We Serve Alumni & Parents Employers Faculty & Staff Students Career Exploration Communities What is a CEC? Arts, Media & Entertainment Business & Finance Health & Medicine Law, Government & Policy Science, Engineering & Tech Social Impact Build Career Skills Apply to Grad School Create a Resume / Cover Letter Explore Your Interests Find an Internship Find a Job Interviewing Network with Centre Alumni Our Outcomes Meet the Team Meet the Staff Meet the Student Team News & Advice Career Resources Student Resources Jobs & Internships Career Videos Our Outcomes Network with Centre Alumni Put the power of the Centre Alumni network to work for you! Career Advocates are alumni actively committed to helping students launch their careers. Networking is one of the most effective ways to make job hunters stand out in the marketplace. Centre Career Advocates: Give information and advice on how to prepare and succeed in their career field Share first-hand tips on interviewing or preparing grad-school applications Provide shadowing opportunities Serve as speakers for on-campus or virtual panels and presentation And more! WHAT STUDENTS ARE SAYING Joseph Falcon, class of 2024 “Career Advocates provide real, in-person connections that are guiding me into securing internships and mentoring for getting that first job.” Caroline Schoenig, class of 2024 “My Career Advocate provided in-depth knowledge about her job and company. So much so, that I now work at her company as a consultant.” Suzanne Bicksler, class of 2025 “My Career Advocate helped me prepare for an interview and gave me inside knowledge about the company’s needs which made the process simpler.” WHAT CAREER ADVOCATES ARE SAYING Robertson Nash ’83 Director, HIV Program, Tennessee Department of Health “I always enjoy the opportunity to lend a hand to a fellow Centre Colonel. I know that I’m going to be connecting someone from my network with a bright, articulate, and thoughtful person. Centre continues to equip students with the same gifts that have stood me in good stead throughout my career. There’s just no substitute for strong critical thinking skills grounded in a world view that encourages optimism and service to others.” Dr. Abby Winterberg-Hess ’05 Nurse Practitioner and Clinical Researcher, Cincinnati Children’s Hospital Medical Center “Making connections through the career advocate program can help open doors to opportunities that you may not have known existed. These type of connections have made a huge impact for me personally throughout my career. As a career advocate for Centre, I really enjoy helping students as they begin the journey to finding a career pathway that aligns with their interests, talents and passion.” Connect with a Career Advocate Make an appointment with your Career Coach! They can provide you with contact information and walk you through how to network with an advocate. Make an appointment with your Career Coach Sidebar Connect with Us Kaitlyn Overstreet Meet Kaitlyn Kirk Knott Meet Kirk Lainy Castañeda Meet Lainy Nate Meissner Meet Nate Career Resources Skip filter options to posts Filter Clear Filter: Filters See More Filters Filter Controls Resource Categories: Community Resources Cover Letter/Thank You Resources Employer Resources Faculty & Staff Resources Financial Aid How-tos & Support Guides Job Search Tools Networking Tools Online Tools Professional Associations Resume Resources Student Clubs & Organizations Student Highlighted Resources Close Clear Filters Networking: Conducting an Informational Interview Share This: Share Networking: Conducting an Informational Interview on Facebook Share Networking: Conducting an Informational Interview on LinkedIn Share Networking: Conducting an Informational Interview on X Copy Link An informational interview is an informal conversation you initiate with a professional in a career, industry, or company you are … Read More Networking & Career Advocates Share This: Share Networking & Career Advocates on Facebook Share Networking & Career Advocates on LinkedIn Share Networking & Career Advocates on X Copy Link View Resource LinkedIn Share This: Share LinkedIn on Facebook Share LinkedIn on LinkedIn Share LinkedIn on X Copy Link Manage your professional identity. Build and engage with your professional network. Access knowledge, insights and opportunities. View Resource View All Resources Career Videos Networking & Professionalism Video post Elevate Your Career with P.I.E Video post Does Your Major Determine Your Career Path? Video post View All Videos Contact & Location Phone 859.238.5283 Email careers@centre.edu Address Old Carnegie, First floor 600 West Walnut Street Danville, KY 40422 CCPD Hours M Monday 8:30 am - 4:30 pm T Tuesday 8:30 am - 4:30 pm W Wednesday 8:30 am - 4:30 pm TH Thursday 8:30 am - 4:30 pm F Friday 8:30 am - 4:30 pm Meet the Team Jess Metzmeier Meet Jess Joy Asher Meet Joy Kirk Knott Meet Kirk Nate Meissner Meet Nate Lainy Castañeda Meet Lainy Kaitlyn Overstreet Meet Kaitlyn Michael Taylor Meet Michael Laura Hill Meet Laura Genny Ballard Meet Genny Bryana Miracle Meet Bryana Sherri Gowins Meet Sherri Phone 859.238.5283 Email careers@centre.edu Address Old Carnegie, First floor 600 West Walnut Street Danville, KY 40422 Facebook Instagram LinkedIn YouTube Footer Column 1 Blog Events Footer Column 2 Jobs & Internships Resources Meet the Team Privacy Policy | Terms of Service Copyright © 2026 Centre College"
    },
    "https://careers.centre.edu/staff/": {
      "title": "Meet the Team",
      "description": "Meet the Team – Center for Career & Professional Development | Centre College Skip to content Skip to AI Search Skip to main nav Search Keywords Log in Sign up Guests Access Handshake Make an appointment Who We Serve Alumni & Parents Employers Faculty & Staff Students Career Exploration Communities What is a CEC? Arts, Media & Entertainment Business & Finance Health & Medicine Law, Government & Policy Science, Engineering & Tech Social Impact Build Career Skills Apply to Grad School Create a Resume / Cover Letter Explore Your Interests Find an Internship Find a Job Interviewing Network with Centre Alumni Our Outcomes Meet the Team Meet the Staff Meet the Student Team Meet the Team The Center for Career & Professional Development (CCPD) helps students and alumni plan, prepare, and promote their careers. A dedicated, talented staff prepare students for lifelong achievement, including: Guiding students through exploring and choosing careers. Engaging faculty to help students connect the dots between their academic and career development. Connecting students with alumni to help explore career and professional opportunities. Providing students and alumni with the tools and skills needed to achieve success. Offering experiential learning through internships and research to complement classroom understanding. With a Centre degree, support from the Center for Career & Professional Development, and a relentless alumni network working for you, there is no limit to where you can go from here. Jess Metzmeier Joy Asher Kirk Knott Nate Meissner Lainy Castañeda Kaitlyn Overstreet Michael Taylor Laura Hill Genny Ballard Bryana Miracle Sherri Gowins Jess Metzmeier Vice President for Engagement and Advancement Contact Email jess.metzmeier@centre.edu Joy Asher Associate Dean for Career Readiness and Executive Director Joy Anderson Asher is an alumna of Centre College and has worked at Centre since 2000. She has an M.S. in Counseling Psychology from the University of Kentucky and is certified as a Master Career Specialist. Prior to returning to her alma mater, she served as the Director of Graduate Employment Services at Spencerian College and a graduate intern at the University of Kentucky Stuckert Career Center. Joy provides strategic leadership on career readiness and is passionate about career success for all students. She has given national presentations on career leadership, scaling career services for students, career data and outcomes, and integrating career readiness into the curriculum. Contact Phone Number 859.238.5284 Email joy.asher@centre.edu Kirk Knott Associate Director, Lead Career Coach Kirk Knott joined the Center for Career & Professional Development as Associate Director in 2014. Kirk provides comprehensive career counseling to students in the Science, Engineering & Tech and Social Impact CECs, as well as alumni and all undecided students. Kirk comes to us from Bluegrass Community and Technical College, where he has worked as both a career counselor and a faculty member. Kirk has a Bachelor of Arts in Psychology and English from the University of Texas, and a Master of Education in community counseling from Texas Tech University. Contact Phone Number 859.238.5286 Email kirk.knott@centre.edu Schedule an Appointment Nate Meissner Senior Assistant Director, Career Coach Nate Meissner joined the Center for Career & Professional Development in 2022 as an Assistant Director. In this role, Nate provides comprehensive career counseling to students in the Arts, Media & Entertainment, and Law, Government & Policy CECs. He joined Centre in 2016 as a Visiting Assistant Professor of Anthropology with specialties in economic anthropology and archaeology. Nate received his Ph.D. and M.A. from Southern Illinois University Carbondale in anthropology, and his B.A. from St. Cloud State University in anthropology. Research Meissner’s research and teaching interests include material culture, complex societies, Mesoamerica, North America, economic anthropology, colonialism, social network analysis, long-distance exchange, lithic analysis, quantitative methods, and semiotics. Contact Phone Number 859.238.6224 Email nathan.meissner@centre.edu Schedule an Appointment Lainy Castañeda Assistant Director, Career Coach Lainy Castañeda joined the Center for Career & Professional Development in 2025 as an Assistant Director. In this role, she provides comprehensive career counseling to students interested in Health and Medicine. Lainy joined Centre in 2023 as an Admission Counselor and also served as the Arts Liaison between the Office of Admission and the Performing Arts and Studio Arts programs. Lainy earned her B.A. in Spanish Language and Literature from Centre in 2020, with double minors in Latin American Studies and Studio Art. Contact Email lainy.castaneda@centre.edu Schedule an Appointment Kaitlyn Overstreet Assistant Director, Career Coach Kaitlyn Overstreet joined the Center for Career & Professional Development in 2025 as an Assistant Director. In this role, she provides comprehensive career counseling to students interested in Business, Economics, and Finance. Kaitlyn earned her BA from Georgetown College and began working in Higher Education immediately following graduation. She went on to pursue two MA degrees from Campbellsville University and is utilizing both in her work today. A Danville native, she and her husband now live in Harrodsburg with their son. Contact Email kaitlyn.overstreet@centre.edu Schedule an Appointment Michael Taylor Associate Director for Internships Michael Taylor joined the Center for Career & Professional Development in January 2023 as the Assistant Director for Career Exploration Communities. As of June 2025, Michael serves as the Associate Director for Internships where he administers all aspects of the Centre internship program, and improves access to internship opportunities. Michael holds a Bachelor of Music in Music Education, a Master of Education in School Counseling, a Master of Arts in Professional Counseling, and is a Certified Career Counselor through the National Career Development Association. Contact Phone Number 859.238.5306 Email michael.taylor@centre.edu Laura Hill Associate Director of Employer and Alumni Career Networks With over 11 years of dedicated experience in healthcare business development, Laura built a career centered on creating meaningful partnerships, expanding access to care, and championing innovative strategies that improve lives. Her journey in healthcare allowed her to strengthen community relationships, drive growth initiatives, and advocate for compassionate, high-quality behavioral healthcare. Laura Hill is excited to bring this same passion for connection, strategy, and growth into the world of higher education. As the Associate Director of Employer and Alumni Career Networks for Centre College, she will partner with employers, alumni, and community organizations to support student development and career readiness. By combining her background in business development with a heart for mentorship and collaboration, she is committed to helping students explore opportunities, build confidence, and prepare for successful futures. As a proud Centre alum, it’s especially meaningful to return to her alma mater and invest in the next generation of Colonels. She is honored to support current students as they shape their paths and help foster connections that will continue to strengthen the Centre community for years to come. Contact Phone Number 859-608-0869 Email laura.hill@centre.edu Genny Ballard Assistant Dean for Career Access and Opportunity and Professor of Spanish Genny Ballard, Ph.D. is Assistant Dean for Career Access and Opportunity and Professor of Spanish at Centre College in Kentucky. She is a Returned Peace Corps Volunteer and a U.S. Fulbright Scholar. Dr. Ballard is actively engaged in international education, community-based learning, and student internships. She has extensive study abroad experience, having directed several programs in Latin America. Ballard is also an active contributor to international research groups that focus on intercultural competence and language teaching. Contact Email genny.ballard@centre.edu Bryana Miracle Marketing & Communications Specialist Bryana Miracle joined the Center for Career & Professional Development in January 2019 as the Employer Relations Specialist, and later took on the role of Marketing & Communications Specialist in 2023. In this role, she creates and leads all marketing and outreach initiatives, oversees the CCPD website and social media accounts, and is responsible for the creation and design of promotional materials for the office. Bryana is an Eastern Kentucky University graduate with a Bachelor’s Degree in Communication Studies through the College of Letters, Arts, and Social Sciences. Contact Phone Number 859.238.5949 Email bryana.miracle@centre.edu Sherri Gowins Senior Administrative Assistant Sherri Gowins joined the Center for Career & Professional Development in 2001 as the Administrative Assistant. As the Senior Administrative Assistant, Sherri ensures that the daily operations in the office run smoothly. She serves as the primary contact for visitors, guides students to their appropriate career coaches and CCPD resources. Sherri also assists with special projects such as the annual outcomes report for graduating seniors, the Law School Fair, and provides technical and logistical support for multiple meetings, conferences, and workshops. Contact Phone Number 859.238.5283 Email sherri.gowins@centre.edu Contact & Location Phone 859.238.5283 Email careers@centre.edu Address Old Carnegie, First floor 600 West Walnut Street Danville, KY 40422 CCPD Hours M Monday 8:30 am - 4:30 pm T Tuesday 8:30 am - 4:30 pm W Wednesday 8:30 am - 4:30 pm TH Thursday 8:30 am - 4:30 pm F Friday 8:30 am - 4:30 pm Meet the Team Jess Metzmeier Meet Jess Joy Asher Meet Joy Kirk Knott Meet Kirk Nate Meissner Meet Nate Lainy Castañeda Meet Lainy Kaitlyn Overstreet Meet Kaitlyn Michael Taylor Meet Michael Laura Hill Meet Laura Genny Ballard Meet Genny Bryana Miracle Meet Bryana Sherri Gowins Meet Sherri Phone 859.238.5283 Email careers@centre.edu Address Old Carnegie, First floor 600 West Walnut Street Danville, KY 40422 Facebook Instagram LinkedIn YouTube Footer Column 1 Blog Events Footer Column 2 Jobs & Internships Resources Meet the Team Privacy Policy | Terms of Service Copyright © 2026 Centre College"
    },
