    "https://careers.centre.edu/meet-the-student-team/": {
      "title": "Meet the Student Team",
      "description": "Meet the Student Team – Center for Career & Professional Development | Centre College Skip to content Skip to AI Search Skip to main nav Search Keywords Log in Sign up Guests Access Handshake Make an appointment Who We Serve Alumni & Parents Employers Faculty & Staff Students Career Exploration Communities What is a CEC? Arts, Media & Entertainment Business & Finance Health & Medicine Law, Government & Policy Science, Engineering & Tech Social Impact Build Career Skills Apply to Grad School Create a Resume / Cover Letter Explore Your Interests Find an Internship Find a Job Interviewing Network with Centre Alumni Our Outcomes Meet the Team Meet the Staff Meet the Student Team Meet the Student Team Career Peer Mentors Career Peer Mentors provide direct support for all six new Career Exploration Communities (CECs) by providing front-line career support to students, allowing each CEC career coach to have more time for personalized, high-level career exploration and discernment with students. Career Peer Mentors meet with students individually and in groups, providing services including resume reviews, internship search assistance, and graduate school information for each of the CECs. They also create and give presentations on CEC topics to student groups. CEC Ambassadors The CEC Ambassador program directly supports all six Career Exploration Communities by providing targeted marketing and communication to students. CEC Ambassadors are responsible for creating peer-to-peer marketing, assisting with student outreach for all six CECs, creating content for social media, and promoting the importance of early and continuous career planning and preparation. Makayla Brown Abhishek Basnet Karla Carrillo Awa Nialing Drame Makayla Brown Makayla Brown is currently a Sophomore at Centre majoring in International Studies and Spanish. She was born and raised in Louisville, Kentucky, where she graduated from the J. Graham Brown School. There, she participated in orchestra, volleyball, and various other clubs and activities. On campus, she is a Grissom Scholar, a part of the Black Student Organization, Centre Firsts, and a cello player in Centre’s Kentucky Music Ensemble. She hopes to participate in the Peace Corps or Fulbright after her undergraduate, and work as an intelligence analyst someday. She is so excited to be working with the CCPD! Drop by anytime during the Career Peer Mentor drop-in hours below: Monday: 9:30 – 11:30 a.m., 12:30 – 1:30 p.m., and 3:00 – 4:00 p.m. Tuesday: 11:30 – 1:30 p.m. Wednesday: 10:00 – 12:00 p.m., and 3:00 – 4:00 p.m. Thursday: 9:30 – 1:30 p.m. Friday: 10:00 – 12:00 p.m., and 3:00 – 4:00 p.m. Contact Email makayla.brown@centre.edu Abhishek Basnet Career Peer Mentor Abhishek Basnet (also going by Abe) is a sophomore pursuing a double major in Economics and Mathematics. Abe is also a Next Genius scholar, the President of the South Asian Cultural Association, and a Resident Assistant. Coming off a Data Analytics externship, Abe intends to pursue a Ph.D. in Economics. He is eager to support students in exploring their career options and educational goals for the future. Drop by any time during Career Peer Mentor drop-in hours below: Monday: 9:30 – 11:30 a.m., 12:30 – 1:30 p.m., and 3:00 – 4:00 p.m. Tuesday: 11:30 – 1:30 p.m. Wednesday: 10:00 – 12:00 p.m., and 3:00 – 4:00 p.m. Thursday: 9:30 – 1:30 p.m. Friday: 10:00 – 12:00 p.m., and 3:00 – 4:00 p.m. Contact Email abhishek.basnet@centre.edu Schedule an Appointment Karla Carrillo Career Peer Mentor Karla is a junior majoring in Computer Science and Spanish as well as a Kessler Scholar, and the Vice President Standards for Kappa Kappa Gamma. As a Career Peer Mentor, she is passionate about guiding students through career planning. Drop by any time during Career Peer Mentor drop-in hours below: Monday: 9:30 – 11:30 a.m., 12:30 – 1:30 p.m., and 3:00 – 4:00 p.m. Tuesday: 11:30 – 1:30 p.m. Wednesday: 10:00 – 12:00 p.m., and 3:00 – 4:00 p.m. Thursday: 9:30 – 1:30 p.m. Friday: 10:00 – 12:00 p.m., and 3:00 – 4:00 p.m. Contact Email karla.carrillo@centre.edu Schedule an Appointment Awa Nialing Drame Career Peer Mentor Awa Drame is a sophomore majoring in Economics and Finance. She has been closely involved with the CCPD since her first year at Centre, and now, as a Career Peer Mentor, looks forward to supporting students in reaching their academic and professional goals. Drop by any time during Career Peer Mentor drop-in hours below: Monday: 9:30 – 11:30 a.m., 12:30 – 1:30 p.m., and 3:00 – 4:00 p.m. Tuesday: 11:30 – 1:30 p.m. Wednesday: 10:00 – 12:00 p.m., and 3:00 – 4:00 p.m. Thursday: 9:30 – 1:30 p.m. Friday: 10:00 – 12:00 p.m., and 3:00 – 4:00 p.m. Contact Email awa.drame@centre.edu Schedule an Appointment Contact & Location Phone 859.238.5283 Email careers@centre.edu Address Old Carnegie, First floor 600 West Walnut Street Danville, KY 40422 CCPD Hours M Monday 8:30 am - 4:30 pm T Tuesday 8:30 am - 4:30 pm W Wednesday 8:30 am - 4:30 pm TH Thursday 8:30 am - 4:30 pm F Friday 8:30 am - 4:30 pm Meet the Team Jess Metzmeier Meet Jess Joy Asher Meet Joy Kirk Knott Meet Kirk Nate Meissner Meet Nate Lainy Castañeda Meet Lainy Kaitlyn Overstreet Meet Kaitlyn Michael Taylor Meet Michael Laura Hill Meet Laura Genny Ballard Meet Genny Bryana Miracle Meet Bryana Sherri Gowins Meet Sherri Phone 859.238.5283 Email careers@centre.edu Address Old Carnegie, First floor 600 West Walnut Street Danville, KY 40422 Facebook Instagram LinkedIn YouTube Footer Column 1 Blog Events Footer Column 2 Jobs & Internships Resources Meet the Team Privacy Policy | Terms of Service Copyright © 2026 Centre College"
    },
    "https://careers.centre.edu/jobs/?stag[]=search-for-a-job": {
      "title": "Jobs",
      "description": "Jobs – Center for Career & Professional Development | Centre College Skip to content Skip to AI Search Skip to main nav Search Keywords Log in Sign up Guests Access Handshake Make an appointment Who We Serve Alumni & Parents Employers Faculty & Staff Students Career Exploration Communities What is a CEC? Arts, Media & Entertainment Business & Finance Health & Medicine Law, Government & Policy Science, Engineering & Tech Social Impact Build Career Skills Apply to Grad School Create a Resume / Cover Letter Explore Your Interests Find an Internship Find a Job Interviewing Network with Centre Alumni Our Outcomes Meet the Team Meet the Staff Meet the Student Team Jobs Search all Jobs Search Skip filter options to posts All Jobs Sort/Filter Clear Sort/Filter: Filters See More Filters Filter Controls Job Categories: Washington D.C. Part-time Jobs On-campus New York City Nashville Louisville Lexington Internships Full-time Jobs Cincinnati Atlanta Build Career Skills: Apply to Grad School Create a Resume / Cover Letter Explore Your Interests Find a Job Find an Internship Interviewing Network with Centre Alumni Career Exploration Communities: Arts, Media & Entertainment Business & Finance Health & Medicine Law, Government & Policy Science, Engineering & Tech Social Impact Sort By: Date Published Expiration Date (Soonest First) Close Clear Filters 224 Featured Recruiting Opportunities 224 Accounting Assistant Next Generation Management and Accounting Services Share This: Share Accounting Assistant on Facebook Share Accounting Assistant on LinkedIn Share Accounting Assistant on X Copy Link Recruitment began on September 4, 2026 and the job listing Expires on October 5, 2026 Full-time Jobs, Part-time Jobs Next Generation Management & Accounting Services Accounting Assistant / Administrative Assistant Next Generation Management & Accounting Services is a professional property management and accounting company specializing in condominium and homeowners association (HOA) management. We are seeking a motivated, detail-oriented Accounting Assistant / Administrative Assistant to join our team in Sunrise, Florida. This position provides administrative and accounting support to the accounting department and includes homeowner accounting assistance, document management, and general office administration. We are looking for a dependable, organized … View more and apply General Accounting Manager State of Wyoming Share This: Share General Accounting Manager on Facebook Share General Accounting Manager on LinkedIn Share General Accounting Manager on X Copy Link Recruitment began on September 4, 2026 and the job listing Expires on October 5, 2026 Full-time Jobs, Part-time Jobs GENERAL DESCRIPTION: The Wyoming Game and Fish Department is seeking a General Accounting Manager in Cheyenne, WY. This position leads a section of 16 employees who collectively serve as stewards of public funds, ensuring fiscal resources are effectively managed, allocated, and aligned with the Department’s priorities. Ensures WGFD grant management, procurement, disbursements, cash management, and reporting meet all federal and state financial requirements. Responsible for the development and monitoring of the department’s $100M+ annual budget. Ensures efficient production in these … View more and apply Compliance Officer Specialized Treatment Facility Share This: Share Compliance Officer on Facebook Share Compliance Officer on LinkedIn Share Compliance Officer on X Copy Link Recruitment began on September 4, 2026 and the job listing Expires on October 5, 2026 Full-time Jobs, Part-time Jobs ADMINISTRATIONProject Manager II (Compliance Officer) Job Codes: 9069Annual Salary: $56,345.82-$96,140.06 Apply: apply through www.mspb.ms.govWork Schedule: 8-hour shifts Monday – Friday 8:00am-4:30pm with variations as necessary.Position Description: The Compliance Officer is responsible for ensuring that the program isin compliance with all applicable laws, regulations, and standards. The Compliance Officermust have a thorough understanding of these laws, regulations and standards, includingstaying up to date on changes and communicating those changes in the most appropriatemanner to others within the organization as needed. The … View more and apply Electrical Engineering New Graduate | Chicago, IL IMEG Share This: Share Electrical Engineering New Graduate | Chicago, IL on Facebook Share Electrical Engineering New Graduate | Chicago, IL on LinkedIn Share Electrical Engineering New Graduate | Chicago, IL on X Copy Link Recruitment began on September 4, 2026 and the job listing Expires on October 5, 2026 Full-time Jobs, Part-time Jobs Electrical Engineering New Graduate | Chicago, IL 100% Employee-Owned · Big-firm resources, local-team relationships, ONE IMEG culture This posting is for Summer 2027 New Graduate opportunities. IMEG is hiring an Electrical Engineering New Graduate in Chicago, IL, to support the design, analysis, and implementation oversight of electrical systems in buildings. This entry-level role offers hands-on design, analysis, and project execution experience, with mentorship, training, and opportunities to grow your expertise from day one. You will support project planning, design documentation, … View more and apply Food & Beverage Server The Dow Event Center and Jolt Credit Union Event Park Share This: Share Food & Beverage Server on Facebook Share Food & Beverage Server on LinkedIn Share Food & Beverage Server on X Copy Link Recruitment began on September 4, 2026 and the job listing Expires on October 4, 2026 Full-time Jobs, Part-time Jobs Essential Duties and Responsibilities To perform this job successfully, an individual must be able to perform each essential duty satisfactorily. Reasonable accommodation may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions. Serves food for guests with high level of customer service. Must understand and practice the concept of teamwork. Maintain high standards of safety and cleanliness in all areas. Must strive to provide guests with a memorable experience and exceed their expectations by anticipating their needs. … View more and apply Math Teaching Fellow with Masters Degree The Lawrenceville School Share This: Share Math Teaching Fellow with Masters Degree on Facebook Share Math Teaching Fellow with Masters Degree on LinkedIn Share Math Teaching Fellow with Masters Degree on X Copy Link Recruitment began on September 4, 2026 and the job listing Expires on October 5, 2026 Full-time Jobs, Part-time Jobs The Lawrenceville School, an independent boarding and day school located in central New Jersey, seeks dynamic individuals to join our community as a member of the Independent School Teaching Residency (ISTR) program, a two-year teaching fellowship offered in conjunction with the University of Pennsylvania Graduate School of Education (PennGSE), beginning in June 2027. We are now accepting applications for our two-year teaching fellowship program for 2027-2028 in Math. Candidates must be able to teach a range of courses from Algebra … View more and apply IT & Operations Specialist Orchard Village Share This: Share IT & Operations Specialist on Facebook Share IT & Operations Specialist on LinkedIn Share IT & Operations Specialist on X Copy Link Recruitment began on September 4, 2026 and the job listing Expires on October 5, 2026 Full-time Jobs, Part-time Jobs Orchard Village is looking for a full Time IT & Operations Specialist. Enhances organization-wide use of various software systems to provide for improvement and optimization of business operations. IT & Operations Specialist Responsibilities: Teach and instruct end users on Microsoft Office applications and general computer use. Act as primary contact for technology problems by OV staff. Track and troubleshoot problems. Contact service providers as required. In collaboration with off-site technical support, maintain technology hardware. Be conversant with software in use … View more and apply Program Manager – Male Only Advocates Share This: Share Program Manager – Male Only on Facebook Share Program Manager – Male Only on LinkedIn Share Program Manager – Male Only on X Copy Link Recruitment began on September 4, 2026 and the job listing Expires on October 5, 2026 Full-time Jobs, Part-time Jobs Salary: $52,000-$56,160 Schedule: Monday through Friday 9am-5pm The Program Manager is responsible for the overall direction and operation of the residential program. This role will provide supervision and rehabilitative direction and emergency on-call services to a team of Direct Care Staff and supported individuals. Advocates promotes a healthy work-life balance and offers many generous perks of employment and room for advancement. We are a strong-knit community that values the ideas and contributions of our staff. Are you ready to make … View more and apply Mobile Outreach Specialist Advocates Share This: Share Mobile Outreach Specialist on Facebook Share Mobile Outreach Specialist on LinkedIn Share Mobile Outreach Specialist on X Copy Link Recruitment began on September 4, 2026 and the job listing Expires on October 5, 2026 Full-time Jobs, Part-time Jobs Starting Rate: $21.50/hour Schedule: Sunday, Monday, Wednesday, Thursday 8am-5pm, Tuesday 12pm – 8pm The Mobile Outreach Specialist position is a great fit for those who have previously worked in a Group Living Environment and who are seeking more independence in their next role! As a Mobile Outreach Specialist (MOS), you will provide psychiatric rehabilitative interventions to people receiving support from the Clinical Team. This position requires significant independent work as well as work with a larger team including a Clinical … View more and apply Pages: Page 1 Page 2 Page 3 … Page 25 Contact & Location Phone 859.238.5283 Email careers@centre.edu Address Old Carnegie, First floor 600 West Walnut Street Danville, KY 40422 CCPD Hours M Monday 8:30 am - 4:30 pm T Tuesday 8:30 am - 4:30 pm W Wednesday 8:30 am - 4:30 pm TH Thursday 8:30 am - 4:30 pm F Friday 8:30 am - 4:30 pm Meet the Team Jess Metzmeier Meet Jess Joy Asher Meet Joy Kirk Knott Meet Kirk Nate Meissner Meet Nate Lainy Castañeda Meet Lainy Kaitlyn Overstreet Meet Kaitlyn Michael Taylor Meet Michael Laura Hill Meet Laura Genny Ballard Meet Genny Bryana Miracle Meet Bryana Sherri Gowins Meet Sherri Phone 859.238.5283 Email careers@centre.edu Address Old Carnegie, First floor 600 West Walnut Street Danville, KY 40422 Facebook Instagram LinkedIn YouTube Footer Column 1 Blog Events Footer Column 2 Jobs & Internships Resources Meet the Team Privacy Policy | Terms of Service Copyright © 2026 Centre College"
