    "https://careers.centre.edu/resources/linkedin-learning/": {
      "title": "LinkedIn Learning",
      "description": "LinkedIn Learning – Center for Career & Professional Development | Centre College Skip to content Skip to AI Search Skip to main nav Search Keywords Log in Sign up Guests Access Handshake Make an appointment Who We Serve Alumni & Parents Employers Faculty & Staff Students Career Exploration Communities What is a CEC? Arts, Media & Entertainment Business & Finance Health & Medicine Law, Government & Policy Science, Engineering & Tech Social Impact Build Career Skills Apply to Grad School Create a Resume / Cover Letter Explore Your Interests Find an Internship Find a Job Interviewing Network with Centre Alumni Our Outcomes Meet the Team Meet the Staff Meet the Student Team LinkedIn Learning Share This: Share LinkedIn Learning on Facebook Share LinkedIn Learning on LinkedIn Share LinkedIn Learning on X Copy Link If you’d like to work on building your skills on your own time in the trusted hands of industry experts and professionals, Centre students can do so, for free, on LinkedIn Learning! This resource offers over 21,000 courses focusing on skill-building for careers and general professional skills. Students can earn certifications to validate their skills (which can be added straight to their LinkedIn profile), customize their career plan, curate collections based on career needs, and more! How to get started… 1. Create a LinkedIn profile If you already have a profile , you can click here to access LinkedIn Learning. If you don’t have a profile , you can schedule an appointment with a Career Peer Mentor to help you get started! Otherwise, click here to create your LinkedIn profile. 2. The CCPD has curated a collection of videos called “Professionalism 101”, tackling the necessary soft skills you’ll need in the career world, as well as important interviewing tips. You can start there to get a feel for what LinkedIn Learning has to offer. To view the collection, navigate to “My Content” and click on “Recommended by Centre College”! 3. Start browsing for content related to the skills you’re interested in! For example: Interested in marketing? Discover courses focusing on high-impact storytelling, strategic content marketing, or SEO. Interested in working in government? Discover courses on managing government projects, lessons in serving the public in government, and government grants. Interested in learning technical skills? You’ll find courses in mastering Excel or programming in Python. This is just a small example of the many kinds of content available to you! Contact & Location Phone 859.238.5283 Email careers@centre.edu Address Old Carnegie, First floor 600 West Walnut Street Danville, KY 40422 CCPD Hours M Monday 8:30 am - 4:30 pm T Tuesday 8:30 am - 4:30 pm W Wednesday 8:30 am - 4:30 pm TH Thursday 8:30 am - 4:30 pm F Friday 8:30 am - 4:30 pm Meet the Team Jess Metzmeier Meet Jess Joy Asher Meet Joy Kirk Knott Meet Kirk Nate Meissner Meet Nate Lainy Castañeda Meet Lainy Kaitlyn Overstreet Meet Kaitlyn Michael Taylor Meet Michael Laura Hill Meet Laura Genny Ballard Meet Genny Bryana Miracle Meet Bryana Sherri Gowins Meet Sherri Phone 859.238.5283 Email careers@centre.edu Address Old Carnegie, First floor 600 West Walnut Street Danville, KY 40422 Facebook Instagram LinkedIn YouTube Footer Column 1 Blog Events Footer Column 2 Jobs & Internships Resources Meet the Team Privacy Policy | Terms of Service Copyright © 2026 Centre College"
    },
