    "https://careers.centre.edu/resources/identify-fraudulent-jobs-opportunities/": {
      "title": "Identify Fraudulent Jobs Opportunities",
      "description": "Identify Fraudulent Jobs Opportunities – Center for Career & Professional Development | Centre College Skip to content Skip to AI Search Skip to main nav Search Keywords Log in Sign up Guests Access Handshake Make an appointment Who We Serve Alumni & Parents Employers Faculty & Staff Students Career Exploration Communities What is a CEC? Arts, Media & Entertainment Business & Finance Health & Medicine Law, Government & Policy Science, Engineering & Tech Social Impact Build Career Skills Apply to Grad School Create a Resume / Cover Letter Explore Your Interests Find an Internship Find a Job Interviewing Network with Centre Alumni Our Outcomes Meet the Team Meet the Staff Meet the Student Team Identify Fraudulent Jobs Opportunities Share This: Share Identify Fraudulent Jobs Opportunities on Facebook Share Identify Fraudulent Jobs Opportunities on LinkedIn Share Identify Fraudulent Jobs Opportunities on X Copy Link Scammers often use job opportunities to collect personal information, so it’s important to learn how to differentiate legitimate job listings from fraudulent ones. Here are some tips and warning signs to be aware of. TIPS If a job seems too perfect to be true, it likely is. Legitimate employers will never ask for financial information or your SSN! Legitimate employers will never ask you to send money or pay for services. If you’re unsure, check the job posting directly on the employer’s official website. Scam job listings often use familiar names and images. Avoid clicking links in suspicious posts as they may lead to fake pages that can look similar to the real site. Instead, visit the employer’s official employment page to verify the listing. Another helpful approach is to contact the company directly using publicly available contact information. If you experience anything unusual about a job posting in Handshake, please contact the Center for Career & Professional Development as soon as possible and flag the posting in Handshake. RED FLAGS Warning signs that signal fraudulent emails and websites: bad grammar and spelling, requests for personal information, and difficulty contacting or identifying the poster. Request for an initial investment. Request for bank account access. Requests for payment or transferring money. Offers to pay a large amount of money for little work. Offers you a job without interviewing/interacting with you. You are contacted by phone, and the number is not available. Vague descriptions that focus on money rather than the job. Email domain that doesn’t match the employer’s official domain. Email domain of a free provider is used, such as live.com, yahoo.com, gmail.com, hotmail.com, etc. Legitimate organizations almost always have their own email systems. Website that has information only on the job you’re applying for, rather than about the company in general. I’ve been scammed, what do I do? End all communication and immediately contact the local police and Public Safety. Get in touch with your bank or credit card company and dispute any fraudulent activity immediately. If the scam happened online, file a report with the FTC’s cybercrime division. Contact & Location Phone 859.238.5283 Email careers@centre.edu Address Old Carnegie, First floor 600 West Walnut Street Danville, KY 40422 CCPD Hours M Monday 8:30 am - 4:30 pm T Tuesday 8:30 am - 4:30 pm W Wednesday 8:30 am - 4:30 pm TH Thursday 8:30 am - 4:30 pm F Friday 8:30 am - 4:30 pm Meet the Team Jess Metzmeier Meet Jess Joy Asher Meet Joy Kirk Knott Meet Kirk Nate Meissner Meet Nate Lainy Castañeda Meet Lainy Kaitlyn Overstreet Meet Kaitlyn Michael Taylor Meet Michael Laura Hill Meet Laura Genny Ballard Meet Genny Bryana Miracle Meet Bryana Sherri Gowins Meet Sherri Phone 859.238.5283 Email careers@centre.edu Address Old Carnegie, First floor 600 West Walnut Street Danville, KY 40422 Facebook Instagram LinkedIn YouTube Footer Column 1 Blog Events Footer Column 2 Jobs & Internships Resources Meet the Team Privacy Policy | Terms of Service Copyright © 2026 Centre College"
    },
