    "https://careers.centre.edu/resources/social-media-tips-for-job-seeking-college-students/": {
      "title": "Social Media Tips for Job Seeking College Students",
      "description": "Social Media Tips for Job Seeking College Students – Center for Career & Professional Development | Centre College Skip to content Skip to AI Search Skip to main nav Search Keywords Log in Sign up Guests Access Handshake Make an appointment Who We Serve Alumni & Parents Employers Faculty & Staff Students Career Exploration Communities What is a CEC? Arts, Media & Entertainment Business & Finance Health & Medicine Law, Government & Policy Science, Engineering & Tech Social Impact Build Career Skills Apply to Grad School Create a Resume / Cover Letter Explore Your Interests Find an Internship Find a Job Interviewing Network with Centre Alumni Our Outcomes Meet the Team Meet the Staff Meet the Student Team Social Media Tips for Job Seeking College Students Share This: Share Social Media Tips for Job Seeking College Students on Facebook Share Social Media Tips for Job Seeking College Students on LinkedIn Share Social Media Tips for Job Seeking College Students on X Copy Link According to a CareerBuilder survey, 70% of employers use social media to screen candidates. Below are some social media tips to think about, knowing an employer could be searching you online. Pause before posting and ask yourself if you’d be comfortable discussing the content with a supervisor. This thought process can help you be mindful of your post and decide if this is the example you’d like setting, knowing your employer can see it. Share posts about your hobbies, interests, and industry-related content that express your personality. Use platforms like LinkedIn to connect with people in your industry or career field. Be intentional when connecting with people online; avoid connecting with just anyone! Curate your feed with people who you’re interested in learning from or networking with. Follow career experts, join relevant groups, and engage in discussions. Share your experiences that demonstrate leadership, professional development, community service, and creativity! Stay civil online and avoid engaging in negative discourse. Make sure you’re representing yourself in a way that a company would be proud of! Always check your grammar and spelling before posting. Contact & Location Phone 859.238.5283 Email careers@centre.edu Address Old Carnegie, First floor 600 West Walnut Street Danville, KY 40422 CCPD Hours M Monday 8:30 am - 4:30 pm T Tuesday 8:30 am - 4:30 pm W Wednesday 8:30 am - 4:30 pm TH Thursday 8:30 am - 4:30 pm F Friday 8:30 am - 4:30 pm Meet the Team Jess Metzmeier Meet Jess Joy Asher Meet Joy Kirk Knott Meet Kirk Nate Meissner Meet Nate Lainy Castañeda Meet Lainy Kaitlyn Overstreet Meet Kaitlyn Michael Taylor Meet Michael Laura Hill Meet Laura Genny Ballard Meet Genny Bryana Miracle Meet Bryana Sherri Gowins Meet Sherri Phone 859.238.5283 Email careers@centre.edu Address Old Carnegie, First floor 600 West Walnut Street Danville, KY 40422 Facebook Instagram LinkedIn YouTube Footer Column 1 Blog Events Footer Column 2 Jobs & Internships Resources Meet the Team Privacy Policy | Terms of Service Copyright © 2026 Centre College"
    },
