      "title": "Jobs",
      "description": "Jobs – Center for Career & Professional Development | Centre College Skip to content Skip to AI Search Skip to main nav Search Keywords Log in Sign up Guests Access Handshake Make an appointment Who We Serve Alumni & Parents Employers Faculty & Staff Students Career Exploration Communities What is a CEC? Arts, Media & Entertainment Business & Finance Health & Medicine Law, Government & Policy Science, Engineering & Tech Social Impact Build Career Skills Apply to Grad School Create a Resume / Cover Letter Explore Your Interests Find an Internship Find a Job Interviewing Network with Centre Alumni Our Outcomes Meet the Team Meet the Staff Meet the Student Team Jobs Search all Jobs Search Skip filter options to posts All Jobs Sort/Filter Clear Sort/Filter: Filters See More Filters Filter Controls Job Categories: Washington D.C. Part-time Jobs On-campus New York City Nashville Louisville Lexington Internships Full-time Jobs Cincinnati Atlanta Career Exploration Communities: Arts, Media & Entertainment Business & Finance Health & Medicine Law, Government & Policy Science, Engineering & Tech Social Impact Sort By: Date Published Expiration Date (Soonest First) Close Clear Filters 2364 Featured Recruiting Opportunities 2364 Assistant Painting Supervisor AHRC NYC Share This: Share Assistant Painting Supervisor on Facebook Share Assistant Painting Supervisor on LinkedIn Share Assistant Painting Supervisor on X Copy Link Recruitment began on September 4, 2026 and the job listing Expires on October 5, 2026 Full-time Jobs Job Overview AHRC is seeking a motivated Assistant Painting Supervisor to help lead painting projects across large-scale facility and office spaces that provide day services to individuals with intellectual, developmental, and physical disabilities. This role is an excellent opportunity for a recent BFA or MFA college graduate or an early-career professional with foundational residential or commercial painting experience. You will work closely with and learn from a Master Painter with over 30 years of industry experience while developing valuable leadership … View more and apply Interior Design Intern DJ Designs, LLC Share This: Share Interior Design Intern on Facebook Share Interior Design Intern on LinkedIn Share Interior Design Intern on X Copy Link Recruitment began on September 3, 2026 and the job listing Expires on October 4, 2026 Internships **Seeking an Interior Design Intern** Denise Jaros Designs is seeking a motivated, creative, and detail-oriented Interior Design Intern to assist with residential and commercial design projects. This is an excellent opportunity for a design student or recent graduate to gain hands-on experience while working alongside an experienced interior designer. **Schedule and Fee** The intern must be available to work approximately **15–20 hours per week**, with some flexibility based on project needs and deadlines. Hourly wage is $15.00 per hour, calculated … View more and apply Social Media Content Creator TOSOT Comfort Share This: Share Social Media Content Creator on Facebook Share Social Media Content Creator on LinkedIn Share Social Media Content Creator on X Copy Link Recruitment began on September 4, 2026 and the job listing Expires on October 5, 2026 Internships Pay: $500.00 – $600.00 per week Job description: Social Media Content Creator Intern (Part-Time, Hybrid) Company: TOSOT ComfortLocation: 245 Bomarc Rd Unit B, Bangor, ME 04401Schedule: 4-5 hours filming on site and editing videos remotely every weekType: Part-time internship (on-site required 4-5 hours for filming weekly), from now till 11/18/2026Compensation: $500-$600/Week About the roleWe’re looking for a creative, self-motivated Social Media Content Creator Intern to help grow our brand presence across TikTok, Instagram, and Facebook. You’ll be hands-on with content … View more and apply Production Intern Wakefield Pork, Inc. Share This: Share Production Intern on Facebook Share Production Intern on LinkedIn Share Production Intern on X Copy Link Recruitment began on September 4, 2026 and the job listing Expires on October 5, 2026 Internships Description Wakefield Pork’s summer internship program is designed to give students a 360-degree view of pork-production. Interns receive the unique opportunity to gain hands-on experience in all aspects of production including boar stud, farrowing, breeding, wean-to-finish, and office support. Our interns are an important part of the Wakefield Pork family and have opportunities to take part in leadership activities, company specific and Minnesota Pork Board events, and more! Organizational Relationships: Interacts closely with Sow Barn Managers, Department Leads, Technicians, Office … View more and apply Communication Intern Wakefield Pork, Inc. Share This: Share Communication Intern on Facebook Share Communication Intern on LinkedIn Share Communication Intern on X Copy Link Recruitment began on September 4, 2026 and the job listing Expires on October 5, 2026 Internships Description The communication intern is responsible for assisting in a range of marketing initiatives within Wakefield Pork Inc. Our interns are an important part of the Wakefield Pork family and have opportunities to take part in leadership activities, company specific and Minnesota Pork Board events, and more! Essential Duties and Responsibilities: Assisting in the creation and implementation of various social media strategies and campaigns Collaborate with other teams, to align social media campaigns and strategies Tracking analytics for social media … View more and apply Operations Graduate Program Amgen Share This: Share Operations Graduate Program on Facebook Share Operations Graduate Program on LinkedIn Share Operations Graduate Program on X Copy Link Recruitment began on September 4, 2026 and the job listing Expires on October 24, 2026 Internships Join Amgen’s Mission of Serving Patients At Amgen, if you feel like you’re part of something bigger, it’s because you are. Our shared mission—to serve patients living with serious illnesses—drives all that we do. Since 1980, we’ve helped pioneer the world of biotech in our fight against the world’s toughest diseases. With our focus on four therapeutic areas –Oncology, Inflammation, General Medicine, and Rare Disease– we reach millions of patients each year. Amgen is advancing a broad and deep pipeline … View more and apply McKesson Health Systems (MHS) Marketing Intern – Summer 2027 McKesson Share This: Share McKesson Health Systems (MHS) Marketing Intern – Summer 2027 on Facebook Share McKesson Health Systems (MHS) Marketing Intern – Summer 2027 on LinkedIn Share McKesson Health Systems (MHS) Marketing Intern – Summer 2027 on X Copy Link Recruitment began on September 4, 2026 and the job listing Expires on January 1, 2027 Internships McKesson is an impact-driven, Fortune 10 company that touches virtually every aspect of healthcare. We are known for delivering insights, products, and services that make quality care more accessible and affordable. Here, we focus on the health, happiness, and well-being of you and those we serve – we care. What you do at McKesson matters. We foster a culture where you can grow, make an impact, and are empowered to bring new ideas. Together, we thrive as we shape the … View more and apply Data Analyst Intern – Summer 2027 McKesson Share This: Share Data Analyst Intern – Summer 2027 on Facebook Share Data Analyst Intern – Summer 2027 on LinkedIn Share Data Analyst Intern – Summer 2027 on X Copy Link Recruitment began on September 4, 2026 and the job listing Expires on January 1, 2027 Internships McKesson is an impact-driven, Fortune 10 company that touches virtually every aspect of healthcare. We are known for delivering insights, products, and services that make quality care more accessible and affordable. Here, we focus on the health, happiness, and well-being of you and those we serve – we care. What you do at McKesson matters. We foster a culture where you can grow, make an impact, and are empowered to bring new ideas. Together, we thrive as we shape the … View more and apply Talent Acquisition Intern (TikTok Shop) – 2027 Summer TikTok Inc. Share This: Share Talent Acquisition Intern (TikTok Shop) – 2027 Summer on Facebook Share Talent Acquisition Intern (TikTok Shop) – 2027 Summer on LinkedIn Share Talent Acquisition Intern (TikTok Shop) – 2027 Summer on X Copy Link Recruitment began on September 4, 2026 and the job listing Expires on December 4, 2026 Internships Talent Acquisition Intern (TikTok Shop) – 2027 Summer Location: Los Angeles Employment Type: Intern Job Code: A188149A Overview TikTok Shop is TikTok’s e-commerce platform, integrated within the app to help users discover and buy products through shoppable content, livestreams, and creator-led recommendations. With teams across the US, the UK, France, Indonesia, Mexico, China, and other markets, TikTok Shop is building new ways for merchants, creators, and users to connect through content-driven commerce. In this role, you will work in a … View more and apply Pages: Page 1 Page 2 Page 3 … Page 50 Contact & Location Phone 859.238.5283 Email careers@centre.edu Address Old Carnegie, First floor 600 West Walnut Street Danville, KY 40422 CCPD Hours M Monday 8:30 am - 4:30 pm T Tuesday 8:30 am - 4:30 pm W Wednesday 8:30 am - 4:30 pm TH Thursday 8:30 am - 4:30 pm F Friday 8:30 am - 4:30 pm Meet the Team Jess Metzmeier Meet Jess Joy Asher Meet Joy Kirk Knott Meet Kirk Nate Meissner Meet Nate Lainy Castañeda Meet Lainy Kaitlyn Overstreet Meet Kaitlyn Michael Taylor Meet Michael Laura Hill Meet Laura Genny Ballard Meet Genny Bryana Miracle Meet Bryana Sherri Gowins Meet Sherri Phone 859.238.5283 Email careers@centre.edu Address Old Carnegie, First floor 600 West Walnut Street Danville, KY 40422 Facebook Instagram LinkedIn YouTube Footer Column 1 Blog Events Footer Column 2 Jobs & Internships Resources Meet the Team Privacy Policy | Terms of Service Copyright © 2026 Centre College"
